            <summary class="erg-faq__question">
              <strong
                >What is the difference between the two registration modes?</strong
              >
              <span class="erg-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="erg-faq__answer">
              <p>
                Single registration is one form for one person taking one ticket
                — the quickest path, and the usual choice for free events.
                Checkout is a cart: one buyer selects several tickets, fills in
                what you ask for, and pays once. You choose per event.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details
            class="erg-faq__item animate-on-scroll"
            data-animation="fadeInUp"
            data-delay="50"
          >
            <summary class="erg-faq__question">
              <strong
                >Can I collect different information for different ticket types?</strong
              >
              <span class="erg-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="erg-faq__answer">
              <p>
                Yes. Questions everyone answers and questions specific to one
                ticket type are built on the same screen, so a speaker pass can
                ask for a bio while general admission asks only for a name and
                email.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details
            class="erg-faq__item animate-on-scroll"
            data-animation="fadeInUp"
            data-delay="100"
          >
            <summary class="erg-faq__question">
              <strong>Can I take registrations for a free event?</strong>
              <span class="erg-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="erg-faq__answer">
              <p>
                Yes, and free tickets never touch a payment gateway. The
                attendee submits the form and goes straight to confirmation with
                their badge.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details
            class="erg-faq__item animate-on-scroll"
            data-animation="fadeInUp"
            data-delay="150"
          >
            <summary class="erg-faq__question">
              <strong>Can I approve people before confirming them?</strong>
              <span class="erg-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="erg-faq__answer">
              <p>
                Yes. Turn on approval and every registration waits for your
                decision. For paid tickets you can also hold the payment — the
                card is authorised at checkout and only charged once you
                approve, so nothing is taken from someone you reject.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details
            class="erg-faq__item animate-on-scroll"
            data-animation="fadeInUp"
            data-delay="200"
          >
            <summary class="erg-faq__question">
              <strong>Can I put registration on my own website?</strong>
              <span class="erg-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="erg-faq__answer">
              <p>
                Yes. The registration form and the full checkout can both be
                embedded in your site with tickets pre-selected, so people never
                leave your page.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details
            class="erg-faq__item animate-on-scroll"
            data-animation="fadeInUp"
            data-delay="250"
          >
            <summary class="erg-faq__question">
              <strong>Do attendees get their ticket automatically?</strong>
              <span class="erg-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="erg-faq__answer">
              <p>
                Yes. Confirmation goes out by email, WhatsApp, or both, and the
                badge can be attached. Attendees can also download their badge
                from the confirmation screen and add the event to their
                calendar. Invoices are emailed rather than downloaded.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details
            class="erg-faq__item animate-on-scroll"
            data-animation="fadeInUp"
            data-delay="300"
          >
            <summary class="erg-faq__question">
              <strong>Can I run an invitation-only event?</strong>
              <span class="erg-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="erg-faq__answer">
              <p>
                Yes. Send invitations, collect yes, maybe or no responses, and
                close the registration page to everyone who was not invited.
                Invitees can bring guests up to a limit you set.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <details
            class="erg-faq__item animate-on-scroll"
            data-animation="fadeInUp"
            data-delay="350"
          >
            <summary class="erg-faq__question">
              <strong>What happens with the data on event day?</strong>
              <span class="erg-faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="erg-faq__answer">
              <p>
                Every registration carries a QR code your team scans at the door
                to check people in and print badges. Walk-ins can be registered
                at the desk and printed on the spot.
              </p>
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <script>
      const registrationFaqItems = Array.from(
        document.querySelectorAll<HTMLDetailsElement>('.erg-faq__item'),
      );
      const registrationFaqAnimations = new WeakMap<HTMLDetailsElement, Animation[]>();
      const registrationFaqReducedMotion = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');

      const animateRegistrationFaq = (item: HTMLDetailsElement, shouldOpen: boolean) => {
        const summary = item.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.erg-faq__question');
        const answer = item.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.erg-faq__answer');
        if (!summary || !answer) return;

        const startHeight = item.getBoundingClientRect().height;
        registrationFaqAnimations.get(item)?.forEach((animation) => animation.cancel());

        if (shouldOpen) item.open = true;
        const styles = window.getComputedStyle(item);
        const closedHeight = summary.getBoundingClientRect().height
          + parseFloat(styles.paddingTop)
          + parseFloat(styles.paddingBottom)
          + parseFloat(styles.borderTopWidth)
          + parseFloat(styles.borderBottomWidth);
        const endHeight = shouldOpen ? item.getBoundingClientRect().height : closedHeight;

        item.dataset.faqExpanded = String(shouldOpen);

        if (registrationFaqReducedMotion.matches) {
          item.open = shouldOpen;
          return;
        }

        const itemAnimation = item.animate(
          { height: [`${startHeight}px`, `${endHeight}px`] },
          { duration: 280, easing: 'cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)' },
        );
        const answerAnimation = answer.animate(
          shouldOpen
            ? { opacity: [0, 1], transform: ['translateY(-6px)', 'translateY(0)'] }
            : { opacity: [1, 0], transform: ['translateY(0)', 'translateY(-6px)'] },
          { duration: shouldOpen ? 240 : 180, easing: 'ease-out', fill: 'both' },
        );

        registrationFaqAnimations.set(item, [itemAnimation, answerAnimation]);
        itemAnimation.addEventListener('finish', () => {
          item.open = shouldOpen;
          answerAnimation.cancel();
          registrationFaqAnimations.delete(item);
        }, { once: true });
      };

      registrationFaqItems.forEach((item) => {
        item.dataset.faqExpanded = String(item.open);
        item.querySelector('.erg-faq__question')?.addEventListener('click', (event) => {
          event.preventDefault();
          const shouldOpen = item.dataset.faqExpanded !== 'true';

          if (shouldOpen) {
            registrationFaqItems.forEach((other) => {
              if (other !== item && other.dataset.faqExpanded === 'true') {
                animateRegistrationFaq(other, false);
              }
            });
          }

          animateRegistrationFaq(item, shouldOpen);
        });
      });
    </script>
